 "subs": [
  [
   4.3,
   8.95,
   "On February 12, 1809, in a one-room log cabin in Kentucky, Abraham Lincoln is born."
  ],
  [
   10.0,
   13.41,
   "When he's seven, his family moves deep into the Indiana woods,"
  ],
  [
   13.71,
   17.43,
   "and his father hands him an axe he'll swing for fifteen years."
  ],
  [
   18.08,
   22.11,
   "Two years later, his mother Nancy gets sick and dies. Abe is nine."
  ],
  [
   23.36,
   27.08,
   "He'll get less than one year of school in his whole life,"
  ],
  [
   27.38,
   31.1,
   "so he teaches himself, reading every book he can borrow by firelight."
  ],
  [
   31.75,
   35.47,
   "At nineteen, he rafts over a thousand miles downriver to New Orleans."
  ],
  [
   36.42,
   40.76,
   "There he sees people sold at a slave auction, and he never forgets it."
  ],
  [
   41.91,
   45.63,
   "Back in Illinois, he becomes a clerk in a small-town general store."
  ],
  [
   46.58,
   51.85,
   "When he overcharges a woman a few cents, he walks miles that night to pay her back."
  ],
  [
   52.15,
   54.01,
   "People start calling him “Honest Abe.”"
  ],
  [
   54.66,
   59.0,
   "Reading borrowed law books late into the night, he becomes a lawyer at 27."
  ],
  [
   59.95,
   63.98,
   "In 1858, he faces Senator Stephen Douglas in seven famous debates over slavery."
  ],
  [
   64.63,
   68.35,
   "He loses the race, but now the whole country knows his name."
  ],
  [
   69.3,
   72.71,
   "In 1860, he's elected the 16th President of the United States."
  ],
  [
   73.76,
   77.17,
   "An eleven-year-old girl writes that he'd look better with a beard…"
  ],
  [
   77.47,
   79.27,
   "…so he grows one."
  ],
  [
   80.42,
   84.45,
   "Before he even takes office, the South breaks away. The Civil War begins."
  ],
  [
   85.7,
   89.73,
   "On New Year's Day, 1863, he sits down to sign the Emancipation Proclamation."
  ],
  [
   90.38,
   94.72,
   "His hand is shaking from hours of handshakes, so he waits until it's steady."
  ],
  [
   95.97,
   98.76,
   "At Gettysburg, the main speaker talks for two hours."
  ],
  [
   99.97,
   103.38,
   "Lincoln speaks for two minutes. 272 words people still quote today."
  ],
  [
   104.43,
   108.46,
   "On April 9, 1865, after four brutal years, the war is finally over."
  ],
  [
   109.41,
   113.75,
   "Five days later, Abe and Mary go to see a comedy at Ford's Theatre."
  ],
  [
   114.6,
   119.25,
   "At 10:15 PM, an actor named John Wilkes Booth slips into their box and fires."
  ],
  [
   121.3,
   124.4,
   "Lincoln dies the next morning. He is 56 years old."
  ],
  [
   124.7,
   126.56,
   "“Now he belongs to the ages.”"
  ],
  [
   128.11,
   131.52,
   "The boy from a log cabin held a breaking country together,"
  ],
  [
   131.82,
   133.99,
   "and helped set four million people free."
  ]
 ],
